# Testing Rules (full doc: docs/component-testing.md)

## Structure

- One `.test.tsx` per component, same directory
- Sanity test: verify component renders with expected elements
- Functional tests: click handlers, hover states
- Snapshot tests: separate `describe('ComponentName - Snapshots', ...)` block

## Snapshot Rules

- Max one `expect().toMatchSnapshot()` per test
- Never render the exact same element for multiple snapshot tests
- Test all meaningful prop combinations (sizes, variants, states)

## Mocking Rules

- Default: use real implementations from `@/libs`
- Mock only: API calls, file system, database, time/randomness, error conditions
- NEVER mock Radix UI components — always use real implementations
- NEVER mock icon components from `@/libs/icons` — use real implementations

## Time-Based Components

Use `vi.useFakeTimers()` and `vi.setSystemTime()` for deterministic tests.

## Workflow

- Run tests after creating: `npm test -- ComponentName.test.tsx`
- Update snapshots: `npm test -- ComponentName.test.tsx -u`
- Verify all pass before committing

For full examples, mocking patterns, and Radix UI guidance: read docs/component-testing.md
